{number: 99}
{title: ‘Tis the Blessed Hour of Prayer}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
’Tis the [C] blessed hour of prayer, when our hearts lowly bend,
And we gather to Jesus, our [G7] Savior and Friend;
If we [C] come to Him in faith, His pro-[F] tection to share,
What a [C] balm for the weary! O how [G7] sweet to be [C] there!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Blessed hour of prayer,
Blessed hour of [G7] prayer:
What a [C] balm for the [F] weary!
O how [C] sweet to [G7] be [C] there!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
’Tis the [C] blessed hour of prayer, when the Savior draws near,
With a tender compassion His [G7] children to hear;
When He [C] tells us we may cast at His [F] feet every care,
What a [C] balm for the weary, O how [G7] sweet to be [C] there!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
’Tis the [C] blessed hour of prayer, when the tempted and tried
To the Savior Who loves them their [G7] sorrow confide;
With a [C] sympathizing heart He re-[F] moves every care;
What a [C] balm for the weary! O how [G7] sweet to be [C] there!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
At the [C] blessed hour of prayer, trusting Him we believe
That the blessing we’re needing we’ll [G7] surely receive;
In the [C] fullness of this trust we shall [F] lose every care;
What a [C] balm for the weary! O how [G7] sweet to be [C] there!
{end_of_verse}
